# Comparison Table: Common Algorithms

| Algorithm | Supervised? | Interpretable? | Scales to large data? | Best use case |
|---|---:|---:|---:|---|
| Linear Regression | Yes (regression) | High | Yes | Baseline regression |
| Logistic Regression | Yes (classification) | High | Yes | Baseline classification |
| Decision Tree | Yes | High | Moderate | Explainable rules |
| Random Forest | Yes | Medium | Moderate | Tabular, robust baseline |
| XGBoost | Yes | Low | Yes | High-performance tabular |
| SVM | Yes | Medium | No (kernel) | Small/medium high-dim datasets |
| k-NN | Yes | Low | No | Small datasets, prototype systems |

---

# Practical Tips
- Always start with simple baselines (logistic/linear + feature engineering).
- Use cross-validation and keep a holdout test set.
- Monitor model drift and retrain when necessary.

